    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm finalizing the catering for a 500-person corporate gala for a law firm next week. We just got a bunch of last-minute updates: we have about 12 people with severe peanut allergies and another 8 who are strictly vegan. What's the best way to communicate this to the kitchen staff so nothing gets mixed up, and how should we handle the buffet labeling so guests can identify their food safely? Thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can clearly mark the vegan and peanut-free options at both the buffet stations and on individual menus to ensure clarity. Use color-coded flags or signs to identify the separate sections. Also, inform the kitchen staff about the severe peanut allergies and vegan requirements, so they take extra precautions when preparing and serving those dishes. Consider also designating a specific area for vegan and peanut-free guests to avoid cross-contamination.",
