      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A formal written document, such as a detailed handout or a standardized allergy guide, is a good idea for the kitchen staff, as it ensures they have a clear understanding of the requirements. During the prep session, provide a verbal briefing to address any_questions or concerns they may have. As for the buffet labels, consider using a standardized format, such as a simple card or a card with a checkbox list of dietary restrictions, like \"Vegan\" or \"Peanut-Free\". This will help keep the labels clear and easy to read.",
